# Vendor data

The files in this directory are **not** part of this project's code and are **not**
covered by any licence of this repository. They are Konica Minolta's own driver
files, taken from the CUPS filter package of the bizhub 206 (the `245igdi`
runtime), so that a fresh install has everything it needs to produce real output.

| Path | What it is | Used by |
|---|---|---|
| `KonicaMinolta/245igdi/Halftones/COPA.DEFAULT.600x600.hft` | the 600 dpi halftone screen | konica-native (mandatory) |
| `KonicaMinolta/245igdi/Halftones/COPA.DEFAULT.1200x600.hft` | the 1200x600 screen | not used by default |
| `KonicaMinolta/245igdi/Profiles/sRGB.icm` | input matrix/shaper profile | konica-native (colour table) |
| `KonicaMinolta/245igdi/Profiles/sGrayInv.icm` | output grey profile | konica-native (colour table) |
| `KonicaMinolta/245igdi/Profiles/{CIELab,cmy,rgbInv,sGray,swop}.icm` | the remaining vendor profiles | not used by konica-native |
| `KonicaMinolta/KonicaMinolta-206-native.ppd` | CUPS PPD, derived from the vendor's `245igdi.PPD` | the CUPS queue; the app's `KONICA_PPD` is optional |

## Provenance

Taken from the Konica Minolta bizhub 206 driver's own installation on the
machine this project was developed on (`245igdi` runtime tree). The PPD is the
vendor's PPD with the ICC-free full-bleed retrofit applied.

## Licence

These files remain the property of Konica Minolta. They are included here for the
convenience of people who own a bizhub 206 and want a working install; they are
not covered by this repository's licence, and redistributing them - in this
repository or elsewhere - needs the vendor's permission.

Nothing in this repository's *code* needs these files: the app, the test suite
(`make check`, `make check-native`) and the whole IPP path work without them.
They are only needed to turn a job into paper, because konica-native loads the
halftone screen and the two ICC profiles before it writes the first byte of a
job and refuses to emit anything without them.

If you prefer not to have them, delete this directory and point
`KONICA_VENDOR_FILTER` at a filter that brings its own data.
